# Files not uploaded to Vercel.
#
# IMPORTANT: these patterns are gitignore-style and match at ANY DEPTH unless
# anchored with a leading slash. An unanchored `src/` does not mean "the Python
# src/ at the repo root" - it ALSO matches `frontend/src/`, which is where
# src/lib, src/fixtures and src/styles live.
#
# That is exactly what broke every git-triggered build: 52 files removed,
# including all of frontend/src, then module-not-found on every `@/src/...`
# import. CLI deploys kept succeeding and hid it, because the alias always
# pointed at the last good one.
#
# Every root-only exclusion below is anchored. Do not remove the leading slashes.

# --- Python side: not part of the Next.js build ------------------------------
/backend/
/src/
/scripts/
/tests/
/run.py
/run_discovery_with_artifacts.py
/requirements.txt
/requirements-dev.txt
/pytest.ini
/Dockerfile

# --- eval artifacts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Large, and the app does not read these. The /evals page imports
# frontend/src/fixtures/evals/*.json, a different directory that must NOT be
# caught here - hence the leading slashes.
/evals/cache/
/evals/fixtures/
/results/

# --- python build junk (unanchored on purpose: valid at any depth) -----------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# --- run artifacts -----------------------------------------------------------
/cache/
/runs/
/data/

# --- vercel cli link ---------------------------------------------------------
.vercel/
